s in it.","冬至時，我們泡熱水澡，池中會加柚子。"]]],"city":[[["n.",["城市","市","都市"],["a large and densely populated urban area; may include several indepen…"]]],"zk gk ielts",290,4,1,"s:cities",[["He is an expert in the area of city planning.","他是个城市规划的专家。"]]],"citywide":[[["adj.",["全市的","全市性的"]]],null,16308,0,0],"civic":[[["adj.",["市的","市民的","公民的","公民资格的"]]],"toefl ielts",3970,2,0,"s:civics"],"civil":[[["adj.",["市民的","公民的","有礼貌的","国民的","民用的"],["not rude; marked by satisfactory (or especially minimal) adherence to…"]]],"gk cet4 cet6 ky toefl gre",1050,4,1,[["He wrote a book about the American Civil War.","他写了本关于美国南北战争的书。"]]],"civilian":[[["adj.",["平民的","百姓的","民用的"]],["n.",["平民","民法专家"]]],"gk cet4 cet6 ky toefl ielts gre",3219,3,0,"s:civilians",[["Thousands upon thousands of soldiers and civilians died.","成千上万的士兵和市民死去了。"]]],"civility":[[["n.",["礼貌","礼仪"]]],"ky toefl gre",12195,0,0,"s:civilities",[["One step forward is a step towards civility.","向前一步，走向文明。"]]],"civilization":[[["n.",["文明","教化","文化","文明国家的总称"]]],"gk cet4 cet6 ky toefl",3459,2,0,"s:civilizations",[["Do you know how many years old human civilization is?","你知道人类文明有多少年的历史吗？"]]],"civilize":[[["v.",["使开化","使文明","变文明"]]],"cet4 cet6 ky",27624,1,0,"p:civilized/i:civilizing/3:civilizes",[["All civilized countries are against war.","所有文明的國家都反對戰爭。"]]],"civilized":[[["adj.",["文明的","有礼的"]]],null,7204,1,0,[["All civilized countries are against war.","所有文明的國家都反對戰爭。"]]],"clad":[[["v.",["在金属外包上另一种金属"]],["adj.",["包层金属的"]]],null,10326,1,0,"i:cladding/s:clads",[["Mary is scantily clad.","瑪麗著裝暴露。"]]],"claim":[[["v.",["要求","认领","主张","提出要求","断言"]],["n.",["要求","要求权","断言","权利"],["an assertion of a right (as to money or property)"]]],"cet4 cet6 ky toefl ielts gre",874,5,1,"p:claimed/s:claims/i:claiming",[["America likes to claim that it is a \"classless\" society.","美国是一个自称没有社会阶层的国家。"]]],"claimant":[[["n.",["提出要求者","原告"]],["",["索赔人","债权人"]]],null,17177,1,0,"s:claimants"],"clairvoyance":[[["n.",["神视","超人的视力","洞察力","千里眼"]]],"gre",32100,0,0],"clairvoyant":[[["adj.",["神视的","有洞察力的"]],["n.",["有洞察力的人","千里眼"]]],"gre",31880,0,0,"s:clairvoyants"],"clam":[[["n.",["蛤","沉默寡言的人"]],["v.",["捞蛤"]]],"toefl gre",10109,1,0,"s:clams/p:clammed/i:clamming",[["It's a sunny 3rd of July of 2025. On the 7th will be the Star Festival—Tanabata—in Japan. This morning, here on Lulu Island, I strolled to Tim Hortons café twice—Iced Coffee with oat milk, then Strawberry Watermelon Sparkling Quencher with a Sausage Farmer's Wrap. I went to the \"Clam Temple.\" On the way, I glanced at the charming bamboo grove. An old man had dug holes beside it to put compost—eaten mangoes and cherries. At the café, I spoke to Greg, the white man who eventually wants to own a B&B in Kushiro, Hokkaido, with his Japanese wife. The native Ainu and marshes are attractions there. Today, head-shaven Greg is wearing a beige T-shirt and beige shorts—maybe a hint of Chabacano?","今天是 2025 年 7 月 3 日，陽光明媚。7 月 7日是日本的七夕。今天早上，在露露島上，我兩次去了提姆霍頓斯咖…"]]],"clamber":[[["n.",["攀登","爬上"]],["v.",["爬上","攀登"]]],null,12625,1,0,"p:clambered/i:clambering/3:clambers",[["Tom is clambering about on the roof, repairing the chimney stack.","汤姆在屋顶一边爬一边修理烟囱。"]]],"clammy":[[["adj.",["湿粘的","病态的"]]],null,19376,0,0,"i:clammying"],"clamor":[[["n.",["喧闹","叫嚷","大声的要求"]],["v.",["喧嚷","大声地要求"]]],"toefl gre",12008,0,0,"i:clamoring/p:clamored/3:clamors"],"clamorous":[[["adj.",["吵闹的"]]],"toefl",29877,0,0],"clamour":[[["n.",["喧闹"]],["v.",["大声地要求"]]],"toefl",0,1,0,"i:clamouring/p:clamoured/3:clamours"],"clamp":[[["v.",["夹紧","强加"]],["n.",["夹钳"]]],"cet6 toefl ielts gre",8228,2,0,"d:clamped/i:clamping/s:clamps"],"clampdown":[[["n.",["压制","取缔"]]],null,32835,1,0,"s:clampdowns"],"clan":[[["n.",["氏族","宗族","集团"]],["",["支"]]],"toefl ielts",5636,2,0,"s:clans",[["The clan system is a key component of traditional Chinese culture.","宗族制度是中国传统文化的重要组成部分。"]]],"clandestine":[[["",["秘密的","暗中的"]],["adj.",["偷偷摸摸的"]]],"toefl gre",11864,1,0],"clang":[[["v.",["发出当当声","发铿锵声","使发铿锵声"]],["n.",["当当声","铿锵声"]]],null,18195,0,0,"i:clanging/s:clangs/p:clanged",[["The kid is clanging away with his toy.","這個孩子正在鏗鏗鏘鏘地玩著他的玩具。"]]],"clank":[[["v.",["发叮当声","发铿锵声","使铿然作响"]],["n.",["叮当声"]]],null,19561,0,0,"i:clanking/p:clanked/s:clanks"],"clannish":[[["adj.",["氏族的","宗族的","团结心很强的"]]],"gre",39075,0,0],"clap":[[["n.",["拍手","拍手声","霹雳声","花柳病"]],["v.",["鼓掌","(使)啪地关上"]]],"zk gk cet4 cet6 ky toefl",6723,1,1,"p:clapped/i:clapping/3:claps",[["Inside the venue, sounds of clapping, whistling, yelling, laughing blended together.","会场内，掌声、哨声、喊声、笑声乱成了一锅粥。"]]],"clapboard":[[["n.",["护墙板","护壁板","桶板"]],["v.",["给...覆盖护墙板"]]],null,16767,0,0,"i:clapboarding/p:clapboarded/3:clapboards"],"claret":[[["n.",["红葡萄酒","深紫红色"]],["adj.",["深紫红色的"]]],null,27173,1,0,"s:clarets"],"clarification":[[["n.",["澄清","净化","澄清报告"]]],"toefl",11316,0,0,"s:clarifications",[["Thank you for the clarification.","感谢澄清。"]]],"clarify":[[["v.",["澄清","阐明","使明晰"]]],"gk cet4 cet6 ky toefl ielts gre",5050,2,0,"d:clarified/i:clarifying/3:clarifies",[["I appreciate your help in clarifying this.","感謝你幫我解釋明白。"]]],"clarinet":[[["n.",["竖笛","单簧管","黑管"]]],null,15621,1,0,"s:clarinets",[["Neither Tom nor Mary knows how to play the clarinet.","湯姆和瑪麗都不會吹單簧管。"]]],"clarion":[[["n.",["尖音号角"]],["adj.",["清澈响亮的"]]],"gre",19890,0,0,"i:clarioning/p:clarioned/3:clarions"],"clarity":[[["",["透明度","透明性","清晰性"]],["n.",["清楚","明晰"]]],"ky ielts gre",5443,1,0,"s:clarities",[["All individuals in the world act with clear goals and distinct intentions. But once these actions are brought together by the great torrents of life, clarity recedes and chaos ensues.","世界上任何人的独自活动，都是清醒而目标明确的，然而一旦被生活的洪流聚在一起，就变得混沌不清了。"]]],"clash":[[["n.",["冲突","撞击声","抵触"]],["v.",["冲突","抵触","使发出撞击声"]],["",["对撞"]]],"cet6 ky ielts gre",6143,3,0,"s:clashes/d:clashed/i:clashing",[["Every now and then they clash over their differences.","他们有时候有矛盾冲突"]]],"clasp":[[["n.",["扣子","钩","紧握"]],["v.",["扣紧","紧握"]]],"cet4 cet6 ky ielts gre",8998,1,0,"p:clasped/i:clasping/s:clasps",[["He held her hand in a firm clasp.","他緊握她的手。"]]],"class":[[["