的肚臍看到我將要出生的房子, 我心想: 我不要到那裡。\""]]],"navigable":[[["adj.",["可航行的","可通船的","适于航行的","可通航的"]]],"ielts",23532,0,0],"navigate":[[["v.",["航行","航行于","驾驶","操纵","使通过"]]],"toefl gre",6416,1,0,"i:navigating/p:navigated/3:navigates",[["My goal is to help him navigate this stage of life.","我的目的是幫助他審視這段人生。"]]],"navigation":[[["n.",["航行","航海","导航","航空","航船"]]],"cet4 cet6 ky toefl ielts",8237,1,0,"s:navigations",[["Early explorers used the stars for navigation.","古代的探險家用星星來辨別方向。"]]],"navigational":[[["",["导航的","船舶的"]]],null,18102,0,0],"navigator":[[["",["领航员","驾驶员","航海者"]],["n.",["航海家"]]],null,16451,1,0,"s:navigators"],"navy":[[["n.",["海军","海军人员","海军军力","烟蒂"]]],"gk cet4 cet6 ky",5950,3,1,"s:navies",[["Mary was wearing a navy blue skirt.","玛丽穿着深蓝色的裙子。"]]],"naw":[[["adv.",["<俚> 不","不是","没有(用以表示否定的回答)"]]],null,18924,0,0],"nay":[[["adv.",["否","不","不仅如此"]],["n.",["拒绝","反对","投反对票"]]],null,18019,0,0],"naysay":[[["n.",["拒绝","否认"]],["v.",["拒绝","否认"]]],"gre",0,0,0],"naysayer":[[["n.",["拒绝者","否认者","老是唱反调的人"]],["",["否定者","投反对票者"]]],"gre",19209,0,0,"s:naysayers"],"nazi":[[["n.",["纳粹党人"]],["adj.",["纳粹党的"]]],null,5391,0,0,"s:nazis",[["It's all grammar nazis up in here.","這裏全都是語法納粹黨人。"]]],"nazism":[[["n.",["纳粹主义"]]],null,16387,0,0,[["What I’m getting at is that Zamenhof not only built a linguistic object, but that behind that was an idea — an idea of brotherhood, a pacifist idea. That strength of an ideal — for which Esperantists were even persecuted under Nazism and Stalinism — is still conserved by the community of Esperantists. One cannot say that it has failed, but one thing needs to be said: the reason why any language is successful is always indefinable.","我想说的是，柴门霍夫不仅构建了一个语言学对象，而且在这之后还有一个理念——一个兄弟情谊的理念，一个和平主义的理念。这种…"]]],"nb":[[["",["注意","留心","铌(41号元素)"]]],null,0,1,0],"near":[[["adj.",["近的","近亲的","近似的"],["not far distant in time or space or degree or circumstances"]],["adv.",["接近","亲近"]],["prep.",["靠近","近似于"]],["v.",["接近","走近"]]],"zk gk",706,5,1,"t:nearest/r:nearer/i:nearing/p:neared/3:nears",[["It is dangerous for children to play near this pond.","小孩在這個水池旁邊玩會很容易發生意外的。"]]],"nearby":[[["adj.",["附近的","近旁的"]],["adv.",["在附近","近旁地"]],["prep.",["在...附近"]]],"gk cet4 cet6 ky",2423,3,1,[["We took refuge from the storm in a nearby barn.","为躲避风暴，我们躲到了附近的一个谷仓内。"]]],"nearly":[[["adv.",["几乎","密切地"]]],"zk gk toefl",599,4,1,[["You nearly poked me in the eye with your pencil.","你的鉛筆差點戳到我的眼睛了。"]]],"neat":[[["adj.",["整洁的","巧妙的","匀称的","简洁的"]],["n.",["牛"]]],"gk cet4 cet6 ky toefl ielts",4683,3,1,"r:neater/t:neatest",[["Tom isn't as neat as he used to be.","汤姆没有以前那么条理。"]]],"neatly":[[["adv.",["整洁地","干净地","匀称地"]]],null,5788,0,1,[["She folded her handkerchief neatly.","她整齊地把她的手帕折好。"]]],"nebula":[[["n.",["星云","角膜云翳","薄翳","角膜翳","喷雾剂"]]],"toefl",8201,0,0,"s:nebulae",[["It's the 26th of April of 2025. Before 14:00, a sunny blue-sky afternoon, I went to my neighbourhood's cul-de-sac to meditatively walk around and around there. I admired the gardens. They reminded me of Daoism: how the microcosm reflects the macrocosm: The puffs of sakura would be a nebula afar. One need not really travel too far. Barb my white neighbour was at her driveway. She and her husband Ken would be going out to buy eggs. They eat many eggs.","那是 2025 年 4 月 26 日。下午兩點前，陽光明媚，萬里無雲。我來到我家附近的死胡同，靜靜地漫步。我欣賞著花園…"]]],"nebulous":[[["adj.",["星云的","星云状的","朦胧的"]]],"gre",19938,0,0],"necessarily":[[["adv.",["必然地","必须地","必要地"]]],"cet4 cet6",1957,3,1,[["Someone who doesn't understand you is not necessarily an idiot.","一個不懂你的人不一定就是一個笨蛋。"]]],"necessary":[[["adj.",["必要的","必然的","必需的"],["absolutely essential"]]],"zk gk",982,4,1,"s:necessaries",[["It is not necessary for you to quit the job.","你没必要辞掉工作。"]]],"necessitate":[[["v.",["迫使","使成为必需","需要"]]],"cet6 ky ielts",10233,1,0,"p:necessitated/3:necessitates/i:necessitating"],"necessitous":[[["adj.",["贫乏的","穷困的","紧迫的","必需的"]]],"gre",0,0,0],"necessity":[[["n.",["需要","必需品","必然"]],["",["必要性","必然性","必要"]]],"cet4 cet6 ky toefl",3951,2,0,"s:necessities",[["Labor is not merely a necessity bu