ound and fury, signifying nothing.","人生如夢，如影隨形，像個蹩腳的演員，在舞台上虛張聲勢、矯揉造作一小時，然後便銷聲匿跡。人生如白痴講的故事，喧囂吵雜，卻…"]]],"stub":[[["n.",["断肢","烟蒂","树桩","残余","存根"]],["v.",["连根拔除","踩熄"]]],"toefl",15097,1,0,"p:stubbed/s:stubs/i:stubbing"],"stubble":[[["n.",["残株","茬"]]],null,14422,0,0,"s:stubbles/d:stubbled"],"stubborn":[[["adj.",["顽固的","不听话的","执拗的","棘手的"]]],"gk cet6 ky toefl ielts gre",7548,2,0,[["I have never come across such a stubborn person.","我从来没碰到过这么倔的人。"]]],"stubbornly":[[["adv.",["倔强地","顽固地"]]],null,13316,0,0],"stubbornness":[[["n.",["倔强","顽强","棘手"]]],"toefl",18393,0,0],"stubby":[[["adj.",["又短又秃的(铅笔)","粗而短的(身材)","浓密短硬的(毛发)"]]],null,15576,0,0,"r:stubbier/s:stubbies"],"stucco":[[["v.",["涂以灰泥","粉刷"]],["n.",["粉饰灰泥"]]],null,12683,0,0,"i:stuccoing/p:stuccoed/3:stuccos"],"stud":[[["n.",["装饰钮扣","大头钉","领扣","种马"]],["v.",["镶嵌","点缀","散布"]]],null,9388,1,0,"s:studs/p:studded/i:studding",[["The stranger who sails for the first time up the Firth of Forth must be struck with the numerous villages that stud its picturesque shores.","眾多村莊點綴著福斯灣的岸邊，優美如畫。初次於此航行的陌生人，必定會留下深刻印象。"]]],"student":[[["n.",["学生","研究者","学者"],["a learner who is enrolled in an educational institution"]]],"zk gk ielts",157,5,1,"s:students",[["My sister is twenty-one years old and a college student.","我妹妹21岁，是个大学生。"]]],"studio":[[["n.",["工作室","画室","演播室","电影制片厂"],["workplace for the teaching or practice of an art"]]],"gk cet6 ky toefl ielts gre",1515,4,1,"s:studios"],"study":[[["n.",["学习","研究","学科","论文","求学"],["applying the mind to learning and understanding a subject (especially…"]],["v.",["学习","读书","研究","考虑","计划"]]],"zk gk ielts",240,5,1,"s:studies/i:studying/d:studied",[["I am going to my room, where I can study.","我要回房间了，在那儿我可以学习。"]]],"stuff":[[["n.",["原料","要素","东西","材料","素质"],["miscellaneous unspecified objects"]],["v.",["装填","狼吞虎咽"]]],"cet4 cet6 ky ielts",996,4,1,"d:stuffed/i:stuffing/s:stuffs",[["There's a lot of stuff in our lo mein.","我们的拌面里有好多东西。"]]],"stuffy":[[["adj.",["闷热的","窒息的","乏味的","固步自封的","自以为是的"]]],"cet6 toefl gre",15048,1,0,"s:stuffies/t:stuffiest/r:stuffier"],"stultify":[[["v.",["使显得愚笨","使变无效"]]],"gre",31382,0,0,"i:stultifying/d:stultified/3:stultifies"],"stumble":[[["v.",["使绊倒","使困惑","绊倒","失足","失策"]],["n.",["绊倒","蹒跚而行","失足"]]],"cet4 cet6 ky toefl ielts",4001,2,0,"p:stumbled/i:stumbling/3:stumbles",[["The newborn giraffe stumbled around on rickety legs.","新生的長頸鹿搖晃著腿跌跌撞撞地走。"]]],"stump":[[["n.",["残株","树桩","烟蒂","讲演台"]],["v.",["砍断","挑战","难住","蹒跚而走"]]],null,7320,2,0,"s:stumps/d:stumped/i:stumping"],"stun":[[["v.",["使昏迷","使震惊","打昏"]],["n.",["昏迷","猛击"]]],"cet6 ky toefl gre",5131,2,0,"d:stunned/3:stuns/i:stunning",[["Everybody in the room was stunned by what happened.","屋裡人都被發生的事驚住了。"]]],"stunned":[[["adj.",["受惊的"]]],null,8857,0,0,[["Everybody in the room was stunned by what happened.","屋裡人都被發生的事驚住了。"]]],"stunning":[[["adj.",["打昏迷的","弄得人昏头昏脑的","令人震惊的"]]],"ky toefl gre",5045,2,0,[["Thousands of laborers and craftsmen toiled for 22 years to craft the stunning white marble edifice.","數千名工人和工匠辛勤工作了 22 年，才打造出這座令人驚嘆的白色大理石建築。"]]],"stunningly":[[["adv.",["绝妙地","极好地","令人震惊地","使人目瞪口呆地"]]],null,17740,0,0],"stunt":[[["n.",["特技","绝技","花招","噱头","手腕"]],["v.",["阻碍成长","表演特技"]]],"toefl gre",9106,1,0,"s:stunts/d:stunted/i:stunting",[["Suddenly we looked down into a cup-like depression, patched with stunted oaks and furs which had been twisted and bent by the fury of years of storm. Two high, narrow towers rose over the trees. The driver pointed with his whip. “Baskerville Hall,” said he.","我們突然向下望去，只見一個杯狀的窪地，上麵點綴著矮小的橡樹和被多年風暴肆虐扭曲變形的蕨類植物。兩座高聳狹窄的塔樓聳立在…"]]],"stupefy":[[["v.",["使麻醉","使失去知觉","使惊呆"]],["",["使昏迷","使失知觉","使保若木鸡"]]],"gre",26072,0,0,"d:stupefied/i:stupefying/3:stupefies"],"stupendous":[[["adj.",["惊人的","巨大的"]]],"gre",21856,0,0],"stupid":[[["adj.",["愚蠢的","麻木的"]]],"zk gk cet4 cet6 ky",2704,3,1,[["My parents keep arguing about stupid things. It's so annoying!","我父母整天都在為雞毛蒜皮的事情吵架，真是煩死人了！"]]],"stupidity":[[["n.",["愚蠢","糊涂事"]],["",["迟钝"]]],null,12078,0,0,"s:stupidities",[["Stupidity is riding a bike that doesn't have brakes.","愚蠢骑着没有闸的单车。"]]],"stupidly":[[["adv.",["愚蠢地"]]],null,19195,0,0],"stupor":[[["n.",["无感觉","人事不省","麻木"]],["",["木僵","昏呆"]]],"gre",19814,0,0,[["The patient is in a state of profound stupor.","患者现在处于深度昏迷状态。"]]],"sturdy":[[["adj.",["强健的","健全的"]],["",["羊晕倒病","羊蹒跚病"]]],"cet6 ky toefl ielts gre",6613,1,0,"r:sturdier/t:sturdiest",[["This kind of cloth is both cheap and sturdy.","这种布既便宜又结实。"]]],"sturgeon":[[["n.",["鲟鱼"]]],null,17256,0,0,"s:sturgeons",[["Sturgeons can sometimes live for over 50 years, growing so large that few predators hunt them.","鲟鱼的寿命有时能超过50年，长得大到少数的捕食者才会去猎。"]]],"stutter":[[["n.",["口吃","结结巴巴"]],["v.",["结结巴巴地说"]]],"gre",14348,1,0,"p:stuttered/i:stuttering/3:stutters",[["When she began to stutter, her classmates couldn't help laughing.","她一開始結巴，她的同學們就忍不住笑了。"]]],"stygian":[[["adj.",["冥河的","阴森森的","幽暗的","不可侵犯的","不可违背的"]]],"gre",38262,0,0],"style":[[["n.",["风格","时尚","文体","风度","字体"],["a particular kind (as to appearance)"]],["v.",["称呼","(根据新款式)设计","使合潮流"]]],"gk cet4 cet6 ky ielts",968,4,1,"s:styles/d:styled/i:styling",[["Fashions of thirty years ago have come back in style.","三十年前的時裝款式又流行起來了。"]]],"styling":[[["n.",["款式","式样"]]],null,10018,1,0,"s:stylings"],"stylish":[[["adj.",["现代风格的","流行的","潇洒的"]]],null,8712,2,0,[["This is not very stylish.","這不是很流行。"]]],"stylist":[[["n.",["文体学家","时装设计师"]]],null,11247,1,0,"s:stylists"],"stylistic":[[["adj.",["格式上的","体裁上的"]]],null,10647,1,0],"stylized":[[["adj.",["程式化的","按固定格式的"]]],"toefl",14263,1,0],"stylus":[[["n.",["铁笔","尖笔","唱针"]],["",["指示笔"]]],"gre",20851,0,0],"stymie":[[["v.",["使(球)处于困难的位置","使为难","使处困境","妨碍","阻挠"]],["n.",["(喻)困难的境地"]]],"gre",15618,0,0,"i:stymieing/p:stymied/3:stymies"],"suave":[[["adj.",["柔和的","温和的","文雅的"]]],null,19685,0,0,[["Gao Dao is usually really suave, but he seems completely smitten in front of his girlfriend.","高岛平时虽然一副很帅气的样子，但是在他女友面前却是一副神魂颠倒的样子。"]]],"sub":[[["n.",["补充人员","部下","潜水艇","胶层","订户"]],["",["子程式","用户","代替","减法器"]],["adj.",["附属的","次级的"]],["v.",["替代","转包"]]],null,1076