taxonomic category consisting of members of a species tha…"]]],"gk cet4 cet6 ky toefl ielts",1171,4,1,"s:varieties",[["There was a great variety of dishes on the menu.","菜單上有各種各樣的菜色。"]]],"various":[[["adj.",["不同的","各种的","多方面的","许多的","个别的"],["s of many different kinds purposefully arranged but lacking any unifo…"]]],"gk cet4 cet6 ky toefl ielts",859,4,1,[["The various dialects of China are what 'Chinese' really is.","我们中国的各地方言才是真正的中国话。"]]],"variously":[[["adv.",["各种各样","种种","不同","多方面","多才多艺"]]],null,13051,1,0,[["Commentators have variously described the sound of vuvuzelas as \"annoying\" and \"satanic\" and compared it with \"a stampede of noisy elephants\", \"a deafening swarm of locusts\", \"a goat on the way to slaughter\", \"a giant hive full of very angry bees\", and \"a duck on speed\".","評論員對巫巫茲拉的聲音作出了各種各樣的描述：除了「煩人」、「像魔鬼一般」之外，還把它比作「一群嘈吵的大象」、「一群嗡嗡…"]]],"varnish":[[["v.",["粉饰","涂清漆于","装饰","使有光泽"]],["n.",["清漆","虚饰","光泽的表面"]]],"toefl gre",15169,1,0,"s:varnishes/p:varnished/i:varnishing"],"varsity":[[["n.",["大学运动代表队","大学"]]],null,10723,0,0,"s:varsities"],"vary":[[["v.",["改变","使多样化","变化","有不同","违反"]]],"cet4 cet6 ky toefl ielts",2371,3,1,"3:varies/d:varied/i:varying",[["In fact, there are countless, varied uses for the Internet.","实际上，网络的作用有着无数的多种多样的。"]]],"vascular":[[["adj.",["血管的","维管的","脉管的"]]],"gre",12123,0,0],"vase":[[["n.",["花瓶","瓶"]]],"gk cet4 cet6 ky",7044,1,0,"s:vases",[["The wet vase left a mark on the table.","花瓶在桌上留下了水跡。"]]],"vast":[[["adj.",["巨大的","广大的","非常的","大量的"]]],"gk cet4 cet6 ky toefl",1965,3,1,"r:vaster",[["However vast the darkness, we must supply our own light.","不論黑暗多麼遼闊，我們都必須提供自身的光明。"]]],"vastly":[[["adv.",["广大地","许多","巨大"]]],null,7509,1,0],"vastness":[[["n.",["巨大","广大","广漠"]]],"toefl",18290,0,0,"s:vastnesses",[["I tripped in the alleyway in the darkness, as I crashed my knees on the asphalt. There was a wooden board that covered a wire between houses across the alleyway. It was very dark there at night. My eyeglasses fell off my face. Luckily, a Cantonese labourer with a flashlight helped me. My knees just got scraped. I remember another time when I crashed on my knees. It was at Don José Heights in Quezon City in the Philippines. There was a vastness of Martianesque red soil, wherein the \"talahib\" grass grew. Sometimes, workers intentionally set the grass on fire. My brother and I were still playing, even then, outside. We were still prepubescent. Near burning grass, I stumbled on my knees. My grandmother, Lola Bebe, was so angry. A maid washed my legs in the big tiled sink behind the garage.","我在黑暗的巷子中絆倒，膝蓋砸在柏油路上。一塊木板蓋著巷弄的房屋之間的電線。深夜的巷弄非常之暗。我的眼鏡從眼睛上掉了下來…"]]],"vat":[[["v.",["装入大桶","在大桶里处理"]],["n.",["大桶"]]],null,14050,2,0,"s:vats",[["If I were a brain in a vat, I wouldn't write this.","如果我的大腦在大桶裡，我就不會寫這個了。"]]],"vatican":[[["n.",["梵蒂冈","罗马教廷"]]],null,0,2,0,[["It's about as easy to start a union in a Walmart as it is to start an atheist club in the Vatican.","在沃尔玛建立工会和在梵蒂冈建立无神论俱乐部一样容易。"]]],"vaudeville":[[["n.",["杂耍","轻歌舞剧"]]],null,17266,0,0],"vault":[[["n.",["拱顶","窖","地下室","撑竿跳","穹窿"]],["v.",["做成圆拱形","撑竿跳过","成穹状弯曲","跳跃"]]],"cet6 toefl gre",8437,1,0,"s:vaults/p:vaulted/i:vaulting"],"vaunted":[[["adj.",["自夸的","大肆吹嘘的","自负的"]]],null,19563,0,0],"vaunting":[[["adj.",["自吹自擂的","吹嘘的","傲慢的"]]],"gre",0,0,0],"vcd":[[["",["可变电容二极体的简写"]]],"zk gk",0,0,0],"vcr":[[["",["长春新碱"]]],null,0,1,0,[["I bought a VCR at that store for a low price.","我在那商店花低價買了臺錄像機。"]]],"veal":[[["n.",["小牛肉"]],["v.",["宰小牛"]]],"gk",12617,1,0,"s:veals"],"vector":[[["n.",["矢量","传病媒介","向量"]],["v.",["(用无线电)导引","给...导航"]]],"cet6",10136,0,0,"s:vectors",[["A vector is a unit vector if its norm is 1.","模为1的向量是单位向量。"]]],"veer":[[["v.",["转向","使转向"]],["n.",["转向"]]],"toefl gre",8715,1,0,"p:veered/3:veers/i:veering",[["The ship was damaged and veered off course.","船體受損，偏離航線。"]]],"veg":[[["n.",["蔬菜"]]],null,31853,1,0,"s:vegs/p:vegged"],"vegan":[[["n.",["严格的素食主义者"]],["",["绝对素食者"]]],null,18638,1,0,"s:vegans",[["I'm a vegan, but my cat isn't.","我是纯素食者，但我的猫不是。"]]],"v